id: curl
name: curl

A one-shot request to confirm your key and llm.birks.dev are reachable, with no client to install.

--- commands (sh) ---
export LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY="YOUR_API_KEY"

curl https://llm.birks.dev/v1/chat/completions \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
        "model": "Qwen3-Coder-30B",
        "max_tokens": 256,
        "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence."}]
      }'

--- commands (PowerShell) ---
$env:LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY = "YOUR_API_KEY"

curl.exe https://llm.birks.dev/v1/chat/completions `
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $env:LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY" `
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" `
  -d '{"model": "Qwen3-Coder-30B", "max_tokens": 256, "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Say hello in one sentence."}]}'

--- notes ---
- A 200 with a chat completion means the key, gateway, and model are all working.
- Swap "Qwen3-Coder-30B" for any name from the model list to try a different model.

--- agent prompt ---
Configure curl on this machine to use my self-hosted llm.birks.dev endpoint at https://llm.birks.dev. Send a POST to https://llm.birks.dev/v1/chat/completions with the model "Qwen3-Coder-30B" and the API key from my environment as a Bearer token. Use the model "Qwen3-Coder-30B". Read the API key from the LLM_BIRKS_DEV_API_KEY environment variable. Do not write the key itself into any file in a git repository, and do not print it. Preserve my existing unrelated configuration.
